1
00:00:04,967 --> 00:00:11,933
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,733 --> 00:00:32,633
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:33,967 --> 00:00:35,167
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,867 --> 00:00:41,167
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,633 --> 00:00:43,833
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:43,967 --> 00:00:45,400
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:46,767
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,933 --> 00:00:48,100
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,633 --> 00:00:51,633
[GUNSHOT]

10
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:53,600
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,367 --> 00:00:55,733
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,533 --> 00:00:57,600
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,300 --> 00:01:00,100
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,033 --> 00:01:02,633
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,133 --> 00:01:06,300
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:08,133 --> 00:01:09,300
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,067 --> 00:01:11,467
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,633 --> 00:01:13,000
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,167 --> 00:01:15,600
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:20,067 --> 00:01:20,633
<i> There!</i>

21
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:22,667
<i>I've only got 1,000.
Can you give me a discount?</i>

22
00:01:22,967 --> 00:01:24,500
<i> You're following me around</i>

23
00:01:24,667 --> 00:01:25,933
<i>just so you can pay
for Rudy's gift?!</i>

24
00:01:26,033 --> 00:01:28,700
<i>When you have the money,
you can pay me back.</i>

25
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:30,167
<i>It feels like it's my birthday
or something.</i>

26
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:31,833
<i> But seriously, thanks a lot.</i>

27
00:01:33,367 --> 00:01:35,667
<i> Damn, you look fine!</i>

28
00:01:35,833 --> 00:01:39,167
<i>Lucas! Forget about
Samantha Jacinto.</i>

29
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:42,267
<i> We have a business to run.</i>

30
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:45,233
<i>They continue delivering gold
to their clients.</i>

31
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:47,133
<i> Raid their businesses.</i>

32
00:01:47,233 --> 00:01:48,167
<i> You can count on us, General.</i>

33
00:01:48,267 --> 00:01:49,700
<i> Don't let me down.</i>

34
00:01:50,033 --> 00:01:51,200
<i>- Ahh!
- Who is she?!</i>

35
00:01:51,367 --> 00:01:52,700
<i>She's my wife.
H-Her name is Gloria.</i>

36
00:01:52,833 --> 00:01:55,200
<i>You don't have plans
to move out?!</i>

37
00:01:55,333 --> 00:01:57,300
<i>No one is leaving,
no one is moving out!</i>

38
00:01:57,400 --> 00:01:59,200
<i> Welcome to the family.</i>

39
00:01:59,333 --> 00:02:01,067
<i> I hope you can survive here.</i>

40
00:02:01,233 --> 00:02:02,333
<i> Poor Gabo.</i>

41
00:02:02,433 --> 00:02:05,000
Now, I'm slowly getting to know
<i> his personality.</i>

42
00:02:06,433 --> 00:02:08,033
Sir, it's been more than
24 hours

43
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:09,200
since we started surveillance,

44
00:02:09,333 --> 00:02:12,200
but our people have been
keeping watch there 24/7.

45
00:02:12,867 --> 00:02:15,700
We've also covered
six barangays so far.

46
00:02:15,867 --> 00:02:18,333
And today, we'll be expanding
our search perimeter.

47
00:02:18,433 --> 00:02:21,400
Okay, so what's your
game plan, Lieutenant?

48
00:02:22,267 --> 00:02:24,667
Ma'am, this is the bridge
over First Creek.

49
00:02:24,767 --> 00:02:29,767
[MAX] Estrella, Gomez, and I
will patrol First Creek today.

50
00:02:29,933 --> 00:02:33,267
We'll cover the areas
we haven't checked yet.

51
00:02:34,067 --> 00:02:35,233
Excuse me, sir?

52
00:02:35,367 --> 00:02:37,367
When did construction
start here?

53
00:02:37,467 --> 00:02:38,667
They just started yesterday.

54
00:02:38,767 --> 00:02:40,233
The barangay captain
had it built

55
00:02:40,367 --> 00:02:42,033
to make sure everyone's safe.

56
00:02:42,133 --> 00:02:43,500
[MAX] Possible exit routes,

57
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:45,400
areas we haven't cleared yet...

58
00:02:45,567 --> 00:02:47,233
Ma'am Altirejos
has been assigned

59
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:49,233
to coordinate with the NCIA

60
00:02:49,333 --> 00:02:51,433
to find out which cases
Sam handled

61
00:02:51,567 --> 00:02:52,900
over the past six months.

62
00:02:54,133 --> 00:02:57,600
Sir, this could be retaliation.

63
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:00,067
All right.

64
00:03:00,167 --> 00:03:01,200
Carry on, Lieutenant.

65
00:03:01,300 --> 00:03:02,533
Men, move!

66
00:03:02,633 --> 00:03:04,433
- Let's go!
- And, Max...

67
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:06,100
I hope you find something
positive.

68
00:03:06,833 --> 00:03:07,800
Thank you, sir.

69
00:03:11,067 --> 00:03:13,767
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

70
00:03:13,900 --> 00:03:14,900
Excuse me, sir?

71
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,433
How far does this river run?

72
00:03:16,567 --> 00:03:18,367
It flows straight to the
Pasig River, ma'am.

73
00:03:18,467 --> 00:03:20,267
It's a wide and long waterway

74
00:03:20,433 --> 00:03:21,633
that runs all the way
to Manila Bay.

75
00:03:21,833 --> 00:03:23,733
Estrella, whatever
evidence we find,

76
00:03:23,833 --> 00:03:25,500
we probably won't find it
here anymore.

77
00:03:25,667 --> 00:03:28,067
They're fixing the bridge.
They must've cleaned it up.

78
00:03:30,167 --> 00:03:36,933
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

79
00:03:38,867 --> 00:03:40,400
[GRUNTS]

80
00:03:41,433 --> 00:03:43,267
- Hey, hey, hold up.
- Come on.

81
00:03:43,367 --> 00:03:45,167
Why are we here again?

82
00:03:45,333 --> 00:03:48,167
We're going to interview the
colonel here, Colonel Domingo.

83
00:03:48,333 --> 00:03:50,800
But the last time we came here,
you two almost got into it.

84
00:03:50,967 --> 00:03:54,467
The last time we came here,
we were just reporters.

85
00:03:54,667 --> 00:03:56,300
He thought we were
easy pickings,

86
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:57,967
so he bullied us.

87
00:03:58,067 --> 00:03:59,333
But now I'm a host,

88
00:03:59,500 --> 00:04:00,833
and I'm wearing
a leather jacket.

89
00:04:00,967 --> 00:04:01,833
Can't you see that?

90
00:04:02,033 --> 00:04:03,500
We're not letting him
push us around this time.

91
00:04:03,667 --> 00:04:05,533
We just need to find out about
Victor Zafra's case.

92
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:07,500
- Come on!
- Ah, all right. Let's go.

93
00:04:08,867 --> 00:04:10,467
- Good afternoon, sir.
- Good afternoon.

94
00:04:10,567 --> 00:04:12,467
- Good afternoon.
- Is Colonel Domingo here?

95
00:04:12,567 --> 00:04:15,133
Make sure you get that
fixed right away, okay?

96
00:04:15,233 --> 00:04:16,533
- Sir.
- Sir.

97
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:17,833
Sir.

98
00:04:17,967 --> 00:04:19,333
Good afternoon, sir.

99
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:21,333
Salvador, what are you
doing here?

100
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:23,433
We were hoping to
interview you, sir.

101
00:04:23,533 --> 00:04:25,333
What is this now, Salvador?

102
00:04:25,667 --> 00:04:27,100
I saw you on TV.

103
00:04:28,567 --> 00:04:31,033
Good job to the NLEA
for the operation involving

104
00:04:31,167 --> 00:04:35,167
Zafra's transfer to
maximum security, sir.

105
00:04:35,267 --> 00:04:37,000
Good job, sir.

106
00:04:37,933 --> 00:04:39,500
Look, sir...

107
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:43,300
I hope you understand that
we in the media do our job.

108
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:46,367
If something's wrong,
we won't hold back.

109
00:04:46,533 --> 00:04:48,333
We'll call it out, sir.

110
00:04:48,433 --> 00:04:50,700
If it's done right,
we'll give credit.

111
00:04:50,833 --> 00:04:51,867
Thank you.

112
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:56,033
Sir, just a question.

113
00:04:56,167 --> 00:05:00,167
Isn't the NCIA in charge
of Victor Zafra's case?

114
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:01,733
So are you in a joint operation?

115
00:05:01,900 --> 00:05:03,867
General Jacinto
had a special order

116
00:05:03,967 --> 00:05:07,933
that the NLEA assist
the NCIA in the transfer.

117
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:09,500
For added security.

118
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:11,900
General Jacinto, sir?
Isn't he retired?

119
00:05:12,067 --> 00:05:13,767
Does he still have the power
to order you around?

120
00:05:13,933 --> 00:05:16,700
Or did he get involved
because his daughter,

121
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:18,733
Sam Jacinto,
is handling the case?

122
00:05:20,767 --> 00:05:22,100
That will be all for today.

123
00:05:22,767 --> 00:05:24,067
I still have a lot to do.

124
00:05:29,267 --> 00:05:30,367
He won't talk.

125
00:05:31,100 --> 00:05:33,400
What could General Jacinto's
reason be?

126
00:05:33,567 --> 00:05:35,733
And could this be connected

127
00:05:35,900 --> 00:05:38,700
to Samantha Jacinto's
suspension?

128
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:42,100
That's what we need to find out.
Come on.

129
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:52,767
[ESTRELLA]
Are there other estuaries here?

130
00:05:52,900 --> 00:05:53,767
No, sir.

131
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:55,933
Estrella, come here.

132
00:05:57,167 --> 00:05:58,100
Ma'am?

133
00:05:58,233 --> 00:06:05,033
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

134
00:06:06,267 --> 00:06:07,233
It's an empty shell.

135
00:06:10,133 --> 00:06:11,167
Take a photo of that.

136
00:06:12,533 --> 00:06:13,633
There's another one here.

137
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:17,433
Here too!

138
00:06:17,533 --> 00:06:21,733
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING]

139
00:06:21,833 --> 00:06:23,233
Take a photo there too. Look!

140
00:06:25,767 --> 00:06:27,300
Forward it to Ballistics.

141
00:06:27,433 --> 00:06:28,633
We have to check if it's similar

142
00:06:28,767 --> 00:06:31,567
to the empty shell we saw
on Soriano Street.

143
00:06:34,633 --> 00:06:36,133
It's possible
that they got here.

144
00:06:36,267 --> 00:06:38,000
But the question is,
were they chasing Sam,

145
00:06:38,167 --> 00:06:39,467
or was she chasing them?

146
00:06:39,633 --> 00:06:43,400
Sir, didn't you say
this current leads to Pasig?

147
00:06:43,533 --> 00:06:45,100
Manila Bay, sir.

148
00:06:45,200 --> 00:06:46,833
If something fell here,
it'd be hard to tell

149
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:48,667
where the current
will take them.

150
00:06:49,533 --> 00:06:51,000
Ma'am, the more important
question is,

151
00:06:51,167 --> 00:06:52,600
if someone did fall
into this estuary,

152
00:06:52,700 --> 00:06:55,600
how likely would they survive?

153
00:06:55,700 --> 00:07:02,700
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

154
00:07:05,067 --> 00:07:06,000
[LINE RINGING]

155
00:07:06,133 --> 00:07:08,333
Villanueva,
bring a forensics team

156
00:07:08,467 --> 00:07:10,167
to Estuary One right now.

157
00:07:16,333 --> 00:07:17,200
Gabo.

158
00:07:18,733 --> 00:07:19,533
Don't think about that anymore.

159
00:07:19,667 --> 00:07:21,867
You'll just have
to excuse Betchay.

160
00:07:22,033 --> 00:07:24,700
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

161
00:07:24,867 --> 00:07:30,133
[MUSIC TURNS LIVELY]

162
00:07:30,233 --> 00:07:35,533
And our neighbors are
doing way too much.

163
00:07:35,700 --> 00:07:37,067
Is that meant for me?

164
00:07:37,233 --> 00:07:39,200
Rudy, they've been preparing
since earlier today!

165
00:07:39,367 --> 00:07:41,033
Someone's even cooking already.

166
00:07:41,200 --> 00:07:47,200
[LIVELY MUSIC CONTINUES]

167
00:07:47,333 --> 00:07:50,500
[INDISTINCT CONVERSATION]

168
00:07:50,633 --> 00:07:53,900
[ELTON] Diday, you know,
everyone's so busy!

169
00:07:54,033 --> 00:07:55,733
They're so excited
for our festival,

170
00:07:55,867 --> 00:07:58,733
and, of course,
for Rudy's birthday!

171
00:07:58,867 --> 00:07:59,900
That's right!

172
00:08:00,067 --> 00:08:02,100
- We should all be happy.
- Right!

173
00:08:02,267 --> 00:08:05,233
It's always fun
in Ginintuang Lupa,

174
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:07,000
especially in Paradise!

175
00:08:07,100 --> 00:08:08,767
- That's right! Cheers!
- [BEER BOTTLES CLINK]

176
00:08:08,933 --> 00:08:10,867
- Rudy's birthday is so special!
- [ESTONG] Of course!

177
00:08:10,967 --> 00:08:14,233
We have to show Gloria
the kind of people we are.

178
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:18,767
Of course, we should make them
more entertained later!

179
00:08:18,933 --> 00:08:20,600
- As we should!
- Yes!

180
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:22,200
Are you going to drink again?

181
00:08:23,067 --> 00:08:25,400
You always make a mess
when you're drunk.

182
00:08:25,500 --> 00:08:27,300
This man's such a killjoy.

183
00:08:27,467 --> 00:08:28,800
[ESTONG] Leave her alone, Pa.
It's not every day.

184
00:08:28,967 --> 00:08:30,800
- Take this shot!
- Yes!

185
00:08:30,967 --> 00:08:32,967
- We're going to drink!
- That's right!

186
00:08:33,133 --> 00:08:34,533
Woo-hoo!

187
00:08:34,633 --> 00:08:36,400
[BOTTLES CLINK]

188
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:41,800
[MAMENG SIGHS]

189
00:08:43,467 --> 00:08:48,067
I'm sorry for Betchay, dear.
You even got berated.

190
00:08:49,233 --> 00:08:53,767
That's why we're trying
to keep you away from her.

191
00:08:53,933 --> 00:08:56,300
Because that woman fears no one.

192
00:08:56,500 --> 00:08:58,900
You saw how mad she was at Gabo.

193
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,567
I mean, she was raging mad.

194
00:09:00,667 --> 00:09:01,733
[MAMENG CLICKS TONGUE]

195
00:09:03,633 --> 00:09:05,167
I know.

196
00:09:05,333 --> 00:09:09,100
And it seems like
she also threatened me.

197
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:10,667
Don't worry.

198
00:09:10,833 --> 00:09:13,567
We are all the same.

199
00:09:13,667 --> 00:09:15,467
You know, that woman...

200
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:18,000
You can't really talk with her

201
00:09:18,167 --> 00:09:21,967
because she thinks
she's always right.

202
00:09:22,100 --> 00:09:24,733
So, if she says something
to you,

203
00:09:24,833 --> 00:09:27,833
just let it go in one ear
and out the other.

204
00:09:28,033 --> 00:09:29,167
Don't pay attention to her.

205
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:32,100
You don't have to worry
about me.

206
00:09:32,733 --> 00:09:34,267
I'll just try to understand her.

207
00:09:34,867 --> 00:09:36,167
That would be better.

208
00:09:37,833 --> 00:09:39,100
Here.

209
00:09:39,867 --> 00:09:42,167
This is how you cook ampalaya.

210
00:09:42,300 --> 00:09:46,000
To get rid of its bitterness,
you have to remove its middle.

211
00:09:48,067 --> 00:09:55,100
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

212
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,733
[BETCHAY] You think
your life here will be easy?

213
00:10:06,900 --> 00:10:08,033
<i> Fine.</i>

214
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:12,233
Let's see how long you can stay.

215
00:10:12,400 --> 00:10:15,833
<i>I'll make your life
a living hell...</i>

216
00:10:17,900 --> 00:10:21,667
<i>...until you choose
to leave yourself.</i>

217
00:10:21,767 --> 00:10:25,967
<i>I'm sure Gabo will go
with you.</i>

218
00:10:27,033 --> 00:10:29,800
<i> And that will be the time...</i>

219
00:10:30,900 --> 00:10:34,833
<i>...I can finally kick Gabo
out of here.</i>

220
00:10:35,767 --> 00:10:38,067
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

221
00:10:40,767 --> 00:10:47,567
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

222
00:11:02,033 --> 00:11:08,767
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

223
00:11:15,800 --> 00:11:16,967
[MUSIC STOPS]

224
00:11:18,633 --> 00:11:19,367
It's Rudy!

225
00:11:19,500 --> 00:11:20,900
Rudy, happy birthday!

226
00:11:21,167 --> 00:11:23,700
- Rudy!
- Rudy, happy birthday!

227
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:27,067
- Rudy, happy birthday!
- Hey, happy birthday!

228
00:11:27,167 --> 00:11:28,800
We're all ready to celebrate
your birthday!

229
00:11:28,933 --> 00:11:32,700
[NEIGHBORS CHEERING, CLAPPING]

230
00:11:32,833 --> 00:11:34,567
Rudy, happy birthday!

231
00:11:34,667 --> 00:11:36,567
We're going to make
your birthday a blast today.

232
00:11:36,667 --> 00:11:38,467
And we've got a special
welcome for Gloria, too.

233
00:11:38,633 --> 00:11:40,967
- Yes!
- And for Gabo, of course.

234
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:43,867
[NEIGHBORS CHEERING, CLAPPING]

235
00:11:45,300 --> 00:11:49,567
It's always so lively
around here, huh, Gloria?

236
00:11:49,667 --> 00:11:51,600
Especially when...

237
00:11:51,767 --> 00:11:53,500
You know,
when there's a celebration.

238
00:11:53,633 --> 00:11:56,267
It's like the Feast
of the Santo Niño.

239
00:11:56,433 --> 00:11:59,333
And whenever someone
around here has a birthday.

240
00:12:00,300 --> 00:12:01,567
Yeah. Look at them.

241
00:12:01,667 --> 00:12:03,433
They're all having fun
outside.

242
00:12:05,833 --> 00:12:07,500
The people here are so nice,
aren't they?

243
00:12:07,633 --> 00:12:09,400
Can you believe
they're all pitching in

244
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:11,133
to celebrate
Papa Rudy's birthday?

245
00:12:11,300 --> 00:12:14,600
The people here really are kind.

246
00:12:15,667 --> 00:12:17,133
But sometimes,

247
00:12:17,300 --> 00:12:20,967
people have the wrong idea
about us.

248
00:12:21,400 --> 00:12:22,867
You know, our reputation.

249
00:12:24,067 --> 00:12:26,467
Sometimes, people end up
doing bad things

250
00:12:26,567 --> 00:12:29,333
because life gets hard.

251
00:12:30,033 --> 00:12:32,467
But isn't that wrong?

252
00:12:32,633 --> 00:12:34,500
Taking advantage of people

253
00:12:34,667 --> 00:12:37,467
and ruining other people's lives
just to make money?

254
00:12:38,067 --> 00:12:40,667
It's good that you see it
that way.

255
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:46,467
Because you,
weren't you jailed because...

256
00:12:47,167 --> 00:12:48,933
You scammed someone?

257
00:12:49,067 --> 00:12:51,500
And you even killed him,
didn't you?

258
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:53,700
- [QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]
- Oh...

259
00:12:53,867 --> 00:12:57,833
Well, I regretted what I did
while I was in prison.

260
00:12:58,533 --> 00:12:59,867
That's all in the past now.

261
00:13:00,033 --> 00:13:02,633
I'm glad you regret what you did

262
00:13:02,733 --> 00:13:04,833
and that you're turning
your life around, dear.

263
00:13:05,767 --> 00:13:06,700
[MUSIC STOPS]

264
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:10,500
[NEIGHBORS CHEERING, CLAPPING]

265
00:13:10,667 --> 00:13:13,367
[SINGING]<i> Happy birthday!
</i> Happy birthday!

266
00:13:13,533 --> 00:13:16,133
<i> Happy birthday, happy birthday</i>

267
00:13:16,233 --> 00:13:18,500
Happy birthday, happy birthday,

268
00:13:18,600 --> 00:13:20,167
<i>- Happy birthday!
- Yo!</i>

269
00:13:20,267 --> 00:13:22,400
<i> Happy birthday, happy birthday</i>

270
00:13:22,567 --> 00:13:25,033
<i>Today, you're the star
Of the day again!</i>

271
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:28,367
<i>So we brought you some lechon,
All we're missing is an apple,</i>

272
00:13:28,533 --> 00:13:31,033
- Then you can lie right there!
- [CHEERING]

273
00:13:31,133 --> 00:13:32,433
<i> Happy birthday, Sir Rudy!</i>

274
00:13:32,567 --> 00:13:35,033
<i>Tall, handsome
And such a good guy!</i>

275
00:13:35,200 --> 00:13:39,100
Neighbors, where's the applause?

276
00:13:39,233 --> 00:13:42,733
[NEIGHBORS CHEERING, CLAPPING]

277
00:13:42,900 --> 00:13:45,200
[SINGING]
Happy birthday! Happy birthday!

278
00:13:45,367 --> 00:13:48,067
<i>When I say happy
You say birthday!</i>

279
00:13:48,233 --> 00:13:50,833
<i>- Happy!
- Birthday!</i>

280
00:13:51,467 --> 00:13:53,700
Sorry, we don't have
any spare change!

281
00:13:53,867 --> 00:13:55,367
[LAUGHTER]

282
00:13:55,567 --> 00:13:57,900
Sir Dante!
Way to kill the mood!

283
00:13:58,067 --> 00:13:59,633
Do we look like we're caroling?

284
00:13:59,767 --> 00:14:01,067
Oh, easy, easy!

285
00:14:01,167 --> 00:14:02,467
Why are you holding a can?

286
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:04,400
- Of course!
- Come on, Mang Rudy.

287
00:14:04,500 --> 00:14:06,567
We're throwing you
a birthday party.

288
00:14:06,667 --> 00:14:09,367
Sir Rudy, that's the original!

289
00:14:09,467 --> 00:14:11,767
- [LAUGHTER]
- That was just the intro!

290
00:14:11,933 --> 00:14:13,733
You want to hear the
whole thing? Here we go!

291
00:14:13,900 --> 00:14:15,900
[SINGING]
Happy birthday! Happy birthday!

292
00:14:16,067 --> 00:14:20,367
Happy birthday! Happy birthday!
Happy birthday! Happy birthday!

293
00:14:20,467 --> 00:14:22,600
Happy birthday! Happy birthday!

294
00:14:22,767 --> 00:14:25,067
Sir Rudy, you're the first one
who's ever heard that!

295
00:14:25,233 --> 00:14:27,200
[NEIGHBORS CHEERING, CLAPPING]

296
00:14:27,300 --> 00:14:28,800
Hey, look at you guys
showing off!

297
00:14:28,967 --> 00:14:31,167
You look even more prepared
than Papa does!

298
00:14:31,300 --> 00:14:33,267
- [LAUGHTER]
- We're more than ready!

299
00:14:33,433 --> 00:14:35,300
We've even got dessert,
black kutsinta!

300
00:14:35,467 --> 00:14:37,600
[LAUGHTER]

301
00:14:37,767 --> 00:14:41,633
[SINGING]
Happy birthday! Happy birthday!

302
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:43,267
Your sugar's going up,
Sir Rudy!

303
00:14:43,367 --> 00:14:44,833
[LAUGHTER]

304
00:14:44,967 --> 00:14:46,733
You know what? So we don't
leave things unfinished...

305
00:14:46,833 --> 00:14:48,067
One more!

306
00:14:48,167 --> 00:14:50,333
[SINGING]<i> Hep, hep! Hooray!
</i> Hep, hep! Hooray!

307
00:14:50,467 --> 00:14:55,600
<i>Hep, hep! Hooray!
Hep, hep! Hooray!</i>

308
00:14:55,700 --> 00:14:58,233
Birthday boy, get up and dance!

309
00:14:58,333 --> 00:15:02,100
<i>Hep, hep! Hooray!
Hep, hep! Hooray!</i>

310
00:15:02,233 --> 00:15:03,467
Go, Papa!

311
00:15:03,567 --> 00:15:06,367
<i>Hep, hep! Hooray!
Hep, hep! Hooray!</i>

312
00:15:06,500 --> 00:15:08,600
Birthday boy, get up and dance!

313
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:11,333
<i>Hep, hep! Hooray!
Hep, hep! Hooray!</i>

314
00:15:11,500 --> 00:15:13,667
Birthday boy, get up and dance!

315
00:15:13,833 --> 00:15:16,600
- [NEIGHBORS CHEERING, CLAPPING]
- Hey!

316
00:15:16,700 --> 00:15:17,667
What are you waiting for?

317
00:15:17,833 --> 00:15:20,200
Go get changed so we can keep
the party going!

318
00:15:20,333 --> 00:15:22,367
- [CHEERING]
- Go!

319
00:15:22,500 --> 00:15:26,433
<i>Hep, hep! Hooray!
Hep, hep! Hooray!</i>

320
00:15:27,500 --> 00:15:29,000
- Umali.
- Sir!

321
00:15:29,167 --> 00:15:30,600
We've got a search warrant

322
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:34,033
for the Zafras' jewelry workshop
in Inustre.

323
00:15:35,500 --> 00:15:37,167
- Yes, sir.
- What are we taking?

324
00:15:37,333 --> 00:15:38,867
Everything.

325
00:15:39,033 --> 00:15:41,667
All the gold, all the jewelry,
records, vouchers, everything.

326
00:15:41,767 --> 00:15:45,000
And if anyone puts up a fight,
arrest them.

327
00:15:45,100 --> 00:15:46,233
This is good.

328
00:15:46,367 --> 00:15:47,833
Sir, when are we going?

329
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:50,167
Right now, before
they can prepare.

330
00:15:50,333 --> 00:15:52,667
General Jacinto's orders
are clear.

331
00:15:52,767 --> 00:15:54,833
We need to squeeze the Zafras.

332
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:55,967
Yes, sir.

333
00:15:56,067 --> 00:15:57,067
Copy that, sir. Let's go.

334
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:58,367
Go.

335
00:15:58,533 --> 00:16:00,500
Jimbo, you're coming with me.

336
00:16:03,433 --> 00:16:05,400
Find a way!

337
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:08,400
We have a lot of lawyers!

338
00:16:08,567 --> 00:16:11,600
Talk to them! Bribe them!
Threaten them!

339
00:16:11,733 --> 00:16:14,867
Use your imagination,
goddamn it!

340
00:16:15,033 --> 00:16:16,067
[DEBORAH EXHALES]

341
00:16:16,233 --> 00:16:17,533
[PHONE SHATTERS]

342
00:16:17,633 --> 00:16:18,700
What's happening?

343
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:21,500
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

344
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:26,033
The local government stopped
our mining operations.

345
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:27,067
Why?

346
00:16:27,867 --> 00:16:29,033
[DEBORAH EXHALES FRUSTRATEDLY]

347
00:16:29,133 --> 00:16:30,067
Pending case.

348
00:16:30,233 --> 00:16:33,600
Apparently, we have
an environmental violation.

349
00:16:33,733 --> 00:16:36,867
- This is no coincidence.
- They're too fast.

350
00:16:38,467 --> 00:16:39,867
Everything's happening
at the same time.

351
00:16:40,033 --> 00:16:43,200
Almost as if there's only
one person behind this.

352
00:16:43,333 --> 00:16:44,733
Ricardo?

353
00:16:45,467 --> 00:16:47,800
He is using his influence

354
00:16:47,933 --> 00:16:52,767
to take down all
of our businesses one by one!

355
00:16:52,933 --> 00:16:53,733
[GLASS THUDS]

356
00:16:55,733 --> 00:16:57,233
What are we going to do now, Ma?

357
00:16:57,333 --> 00:17:00,433
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

358
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:02,733
He had
our mining company closed.

359
00:17:03,733 --> 00:17:05,900
However, our other businesses
should not stop running.

360
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,067
We'll move the gold
some other way.

361
00:17:15,433 --> 00:17:17,133
[LAUGHTER]

362
00:17:17,300 --> 00:17:18,767
- They're here.
- [GABO] Oh!

363
00:17:18,867 --> 00:17:22,100
That smells so good!
Auntie, what are you cooking?

364
00:17:22,267 --> 00:17:25,000
I taught her how to make lumpia!

365
00:17:25,133 --> 00:17:28,333
Love, it seems your<i> lumpia
</i>is very delicious.

366
00:17:28,467 --> 00:17:30,600
- I hope so.
- [CHUCKLING]

367
00:17:30,767 --> 00:17:33,933
[DANTE] Wow, you're really like
a housewife, Gloria.

368
00:17:34,100 --> 00:17:35,633
- [RUDY] This man, really.
- [DANTE CHUCKLING]

369
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:40,100
[MAMENG] Of course!
She's Gabo's wife, right?

370
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:41,933
- See?
- [DANTE CHUCKLING]

371
00:17:42,100 --> 00:17:46,100
[SAM] Pa, we made<i> lumpia,
</i>and I'll also cook pansit

372
00:17:46,267 --> 00:17:47,600
for your birthday.

373
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:50,300
Thank you, Gloria. Oh.

374
00:17:51,300 --> 00:17:53,000
Thank you, dear.
You shouldn't have bothered.

375
00:17:54,900 --> 00:17:56,000
It's fine.

376
00:17:56,167 --> 00:17:58,967
This is all I can give
for your birthday.

377
00:17:59,067 --> 00:18:01,767
- Thank you very much.
- [GABO] Pa.

378
00:18:01,867 --> 00:18:03,633
What are you waiting for?
Go take a bath!

379
00:18:03,800 --> 00:18:06,600
Wear your new polo,
so you'll be very handsome!

380
00:18:06,700 --> 00:18:07,967
- You're right.
- [CHUCKLING]

381
00:18:08,133 --> 00:18:11,167
- [RUDY] I'll take a bath now.
- Go on, Rudy!

382
00:18:11,333 --> 00:18:12,433
- Hurry!
- I'll have to wear this.

383
00:18:12,533 --> 00:18:13,367
I think it suits me so much!

384
00:18:13,500 --> 00:18:15,467
- I'll take a bath now.
- Alright.

385
00:18:15,567 --> 00:18:17,533
Go on.
The visitors are arriving soon.

386
00:18:17,667 --> 00:18:19,467
Dear, don't put it on high heat.

387
00:18:19,567 --> 00:18:21,033
- [SAM] Yes.
- I'll leave you for now.

388
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:22,333
Hey, help me.

389
00:18:22,500 --> 00:18:25,700
Let's get our clothes out
for the party.

390
00:18:25,867 --> 00:18:28,133
- I'll leave you. Let's go.
- Alright.

391
00:18:28,233 --> 00:18:30,733
- Uh, love?
- Hm?

392
00:18:30,867 --> 00:18:32,900
I also bought you
a new dress.

393
00:18:33,700 --> 00:18:36,167
I just want you
to be very beautiful

394
00:18:36,333 --> 00:18:37,533
during Papa's birthday later.

395
00:18:37,700 --> 00:18:38,967
Wait, I'll go get it!

396
00:18:41,233 --> 00:18:42,533
[SAM] He's kind.

397
00:18:43,533 --> 00:18:45,200
<i>He even remembered
to buy me a dress.</i>

398
00:18:47,367 --> 00:18:49,167
[GABO] Love? Love?

399
00:18:49,933 --> 00:18:51,533
I also bought you other clothes.

400
00:18:51,700 --> 00:18:55,300
I bought them when
I bought Papa's polo yesterday.

401
00:18:55,433 --> 00:18:56,600
I hope you like them.

402
00:18:57,567 --> 00:19:00,700
- Hm?
- Here, look! This suits you.

403
00:19:00,867 --> 00:19:04,167
I remembered
you're still wearing my clothes.

404
00:19:04,267 --> 00:19:07,200
Thank you.
You shouldn't have bothered.

405
00:19:07,300 --> 00:19:08,367
And, love...

406
00:19:08,533 --> 00:19:10,533
[PLASTIC RUSTLING]

407
00:19:10,700 --> 00:19:12,033
I bought you...

408
00:19:12,933 --> 00:19:15,367
...a pretty dress
for the party later.

409
00:19:17,367 --> 00:19:19,000
Check to see if it fits you.

410
00:19:20,767 --> 00:19:22,600
Thank you. This is beautiful!

411
00:19:23,433 --> 00:19:27,533
- Wasn't this expensive?
- Yeah, it was!

412
00:19:27,633 --> 00:19:29,100
- How much was it?
- 300 pesos!

413
00:19:29,300 --> 00:19:31,200
- It's from the thrift store.
- This is only 300 pesos?

414
00:19:31,300 --> 00:19:32,533
Yes!

415
00:19:32,633 --> 00:19:35,300
The vendor told me that
dress's owner recently died,

416
00:19:35,467 --> 00:19:37,633
so she sold it to me
for a cheaper price.

417
00:19:37,800 --> 00:19:41,100
It even had blotches of blood,
but she cleaned it up!

418
00:19:41,233 --> 00:19:42,467
[SAM STUTTERS, SIGHS]

419
00:19:43,300 --> 00:19:44,900
- Thank you.
- Oh, love.

420
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:48,133
I'll take a bath now,
so, later, when we're together,

421
00:19:48,300 --> 00:19:50,367
I'll be handsome.
[LAUGHS]

422
00:19:50,467 --> 00:19:52,600
Alright? Then you take a bath.

423
00:19:52,733 --> 00:19:54,367
- Okay.
- Love you.

424
00:19:54,467 --> 00:19:55,533
[GABO GIGGLES]

425
00:19:56,633 --> 00:19:57,733
[SAM SIGHS]

426
00:19:59,600 --> 00:20:06,600
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

427
00:20:12,133 --> 00:20:13,633
[DELGADO] So, Karen...

428
00:20:13,767 --> 00:20:15,800
what do you want us
to talk about?

429
00:20:15,933 --> 00:20:19,133
Sir, I know we've been
looking for Sam nonstop.

430
00:20:19,300 --> 00:20:22,633
Yes, our agents have been
on the ground 24/7

431
00:20:22,800 --> 00:20:26,767
investigating and searching
for your friend.

432
00:20:26,867 --> 00:20:28,733
But can I be honest
with you, sir?

433
00:20:28,833 --> 00:20:31,067
Of course, Karen. Of course.

434
00:20:31,167 --> 00:20:34,633
I don't know if I should hold
a grudge against the agency.

435
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:36,433
For letting Sam down.

436
00:20:36,533 --> 00:20:38,667
Or maybe we had shortcomings.

437
00:20:38,800 --> 00:20:42,167
Or perhaps the enemies
just play really dirty.

438
00:20:42,333 --> 00:20:44,967
We may have had lapses,

439
00:20:45,533 --> 00:20:50,433
but I'm certain
the Zafras play dirty.

440
00:20:50,533 --> 00:20:53,167
It's as if they managed
to read our moves.

441
00:20:53,333 --> 00:20:55,167
The transfer of Mr. Chan,

442
00:20:55,300 --> 00:20:56,333
Sam's actions.

443
00:20:56,533 --> 00:21:00,500
It's possible they're still
tracking our moves even now.

444
00:21:00,667 --> 00:21:02,367
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

445
00:21:02,533 --> 00:21:03,700
You know...

446
00:21:04,233 --> 00:21:04,833
[SMACKS LIPS]

447
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:06,833
We have the same observations.

448
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:10,167
Look, I'm not dismissing
any of this.

449
00:21:10,733 --> 00:21:12,000
Thank you, sir.

450
00:21:17,100 --> 00:21:17,833
[DOOR OPENS]

451
00:21:17,933 --> 00:21:25,000
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

452
00:21:26,233 --> 00:21:27,633
Good morning, ma'am.

453
00:21:37,700 --> 00:21:38,867
[PIA] Sir?

454
00:21:39,733 --> 00:21:45,067
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

455
00:21:45,267 --> 00:21:46,233
[DELGADO] Uh, Pia.

456
00:21:46,367 --> 00:21:48,067
Any update...

457
00:21:49,100 --> 00:21:51,067
on the investigation
I asked you to do?

458
00:21:51,200 --> 00:21:54,533
The one about the possible spy
of the Zafras?

459
00:21:55,033 --> 00:21:56,433
I'm still working on it.

460
00:21:57,267 --> 00:21:59,700
Sir, I saw Karen come out
of your office.

461
00:21:59,800 --> 00:22:05,167
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

462
00:22:05,267 --> 00:22:06,333
What about her?

463
00:22:06,900 --> 00:22:09,867
Do you think Sam was betrayed

464
00:22:09,967 --> 00:22:13,400
by the very person closest
to her?

465
00:22:13,567 --> 00:22:14,400
[PIA] Sir...

466
00:22:14,567 --> 00:22:16,567
I'm not crossing anyone
off my list

467
00:22:16,733 --> 00:22:19,233
while my investigation
is ongoing.

468
00:22:19,833 --> 00:22:21,633
But sometimes...

469
00:22:21,800 --> 00:22:23,433
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

470
00:22:23,567 --> 00:22:27,267
...the same people we trust
end up stabbing us in the back.

471
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:30,767
And that is
the most painful part.

472
00:22:31,733 --> 00:22:32,900
Right?

473
00:22:39,267 --> 00:22:41,233
[DOOR CLOSES]

474
00:22:44,333 --> 00:22:48,767
[PIA] I'll destroy Team Alpha's
trust in each other.

475
00:22:49,367 --> 00:22:51,500
<i>Not only will it slow down
their investigation,</i>

476
00:22:51,667 --> 00:22:56,467
<i>but it will also make it easier
for me to manipulate the agency.</i>

477
00:22:56,600 --> 00:22:59,567
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

478
00:22:59,867 --> 00:23:02,733
<i> Then I can free Victor Zafra.</i>

479
00:23:02,833 --> 00:23:04,467
[SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

480
00:23:04,633 --> 00:23:05,967
[TELEPHONE RINGING
IN DISTANCE]

481
00:23:13,667 --> 00:23:14,800
[SOFT THUD]

482
00:23:18,933 --> 00:23:25,967
[SINISTER MUSIC CONTINUES]

483
00:23:27,967 --> 00:23:29,267
[PAPER RUSTLES]

484
00:23:35,700 --> 00:23:37,933
[MUSIC FADES]

485
00:23:38,700 --> 00:23:45,833
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

486
00:24:01,900 --> 00:24:09,000
[LIVELY MUSIC PLAYING]

487
00:24:23,900 --> 00:24:27,467
[LIVELY MUSIC CONTINUES]

488
00:24:27,567 --> 00:24:28,700
[NEIGHBORS CHEERING]

489
00:24:28,900 --> 00:24:29,833
- [GABO] Come on, Pa!
- [TOLITS] Hey!

490
00:24:29,933 --> 00:24:31,533
- It's the birthday boy!
- Look at your guests!

491
00:24:31,633 --> 00:24:32,933
Everyone is here!

492
00:24:33,100 --> 00:24:34,400
- Mister Rudy is here!
- Mister Rudy!

493
00:24:34,533 --> 00:24:35,533
Time to drink!

494
00:24:35,633 --> 00:24:36,700
- Come on!
- Let's drink!

495
00:24:36,800 --> 00:24:38,567
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER, LAUGHTER]

496
00:24:38,700 --> 00:24:40,700
- [ALL CHANTING] Rudy! Rudy!
- Are you guys ready?

497
00:24:40,800 --> 00:24:43,900
Rudy! Rudy! Rudy! Rudy!

498
00:24:44,033 --> 00:24:45,733
[DIDAY] Looking handsome today,
aren't we?

499
00:24:45,900 --> 00:24:47,833
Your button-down shirt
looks perfect on you!

500
00:24:47,933 --> 00:24:49,567
You know, Gabo gave this to me.

501
00:24:49,733 --> 00:24:50,533
Nice, right?

502
00:24:50,633 --> 00:24:52,667
- Yeah!
- [KULAS] Rudy, beer!

503
00:24:52,767 --> 00:24:53,900
Oh, thanks.

504
00:24:54,300 --> 00:24:56,833
Wow! That watch looks expensive!

505
00:24:56,933 --> 00:24:58,100
Is that a gift from Gabo?

506
00:24:58,267 --> 00:25:00,267
No, but it really is pricey.

507
00:25:00,433 --> 00:25:02,933
Betchay gave this to me.
Nice, right?

508
00:25:03,133 --> 00:25:04,600
- [CHUCKLES]
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]

509
00:25:04,733 --> 00:25:05,933
What are we waiting for?

510
00:25:06,067 --> 00:25:07,400
Time to drink!

511
00:25:07,500 --> 00:25:08,400
[OVERLAPPING CHEER]

512
00:25:08,567 --> 00:25:10,967
[ALL CHANTING]
Time to drink! Time to drink!

513
00:25:11,133 --> 00:25:13,367
- [DANTE] Bring out the food!
- Time to drink!

514
00:25:13,467 --> 00:25:14,267
Time to drink!

515
00:25:14,467 --> 00:25:16,800
Sing for us, Gabo!
Come on, get up here!

516
00:25:16,967 --> 00:25:19,067
I'll sing for my father later!

517
00:25:19,167 --> 00:25:23,933
[ALL CHEERING, WHOOPING]

518
00:25:24,067 --> 00:25:25,433
[TOLITS] Mister Rudy,
this is for you!

519
00:25:25,600 --> 00:25:27,133
We love you so much!

520
00:25:27,300 --> 00:25:31,900
[ALL CHANTING] Mister Rudy!
Mister Rudy! Mister Rudy!

521
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:33,567
[BONG] We love you, Mister Rudy!

522
00:25:40,467 --> 00:25:41,500
[ALL] Happy birthday!

523
00:25:41,667 --> 00:25:42,500
Thank you!

524
00:25:42,667 --> 00:25:48,600
- [CHEERING, WHOOPING]
- [BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

525
00:25:48,700 --> 00:25:49,667
Mister Rudy!

526
00:25:49,833 --> 00:25:52,233
- We love you, Mister Rudy!
- Thank you!

527
00:25:52,700 --> 00:25:54,333
Thank you, everyone!

528
00:25:55,467 --> 00:25:58,167
Girls, boys, lesbians,
and gays...

529
00:25:58,333 --> 00:25:59,900
Young and old...

530
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:02,000
With teeth or without...

531
00:26:02,167 --> 00:26:04,467
The gays are here...

532
00:26:04,633 --> 00:26:06,967
...together with Tekla!

533
00:26:07,133 --> 00:26:14,133
- [CHEERING, APPLAUSE]
- [UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

534
00:26:19,367 --> 00:26:20,867
I'm here!

535
00:26:21,033 --> 00:26:22,600
[ALL CHEERING, CLAPPING]

536
00:26:28,800 --> 00:26:31,767
[UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]

537
00:26:31,867 --> 00:26:34,600
[CHANTING] Tekla! Tekla! Tekla!

538
00:26:34,700 --> 00:26:36,200
Tekla!

539
00:26:39,467 --> 00:26:43,833
[CHEERING, APPLAUSE]

540
00:26:44,000 --> 00:26:45,367
[TOLITS] Tekla!

541
00:26:45,500 --> 00:26:47,233
- That's your color, huh?
- Where's the cake?

542
00:26:47,400 --> 00:26:49,000
It's right here!

543
00:26:49,100 --> 00:26:52,000
Happy birthday, Daddy Rudy!

544
00:26:52,100 --> 00:26:53,667
Here's your cake!

545
00:26:53,767 --> 00:26:55,367
- Thank you.
- Happy birthday!

546
00:26:55,500 --> 00:26:56,633
You're welcome!

547
00:26:56,733 --> 00:26:58,167
- Look at her!
- Whoa!

548
00:26:58,267 --> 00:26:59,000
Gabo...

549
00:26:59,100 --> 00:27:00,233
[ALL TEASING]

550
00:27:00,400 --> 00:27:01,467
What's up, Gabo?

551
00:27:02,533 --> 00:27:04,133
Did you miss me, Gabo?

552
00:27:04,233 --> 00:27:06,200
Sorry, I didn't have time
to prepare.

553
00:27:06,367 --> 00:27:08,067
[IPE] Wow, and you call that
not prepared?

554
00:27:08,233 --> 00:27:10,133
Tekla, you even went
through the trouble.

555
00:27:10,233 --> 00:27:11,233
- What?!
- It's just Papa's birthday.

556
00:27:11,400 --> 00:27:13,867
Come on, Gabo! I didn't
prepare anything at all!

557
00:27:14,033 --> 00:27:15,367
I didn't go through any trouble
for this!

558
00:27:15,500 --> 00:27:17,633
But when it comes to you,
I always go all-in!

559
00:27:17,767 --> 00:27:20,400
[LAUGHTER]

560
00:27:20,567 --> 00:27:25,500
[TEKLA] Oh, our surprises
for Daddy Rudy don't end here!

561
00:27:25,600 --> 00:27:28,000
- Wait, there's more?
- Let's all say "Daddy Rudy!"

562
00:27:28,100 --> 00:27:29,700
- Daddy Rudy!
- Daddy Rudy!

563
00:27:29,800 --> 00:27:32,733
[TEKLA] Girls, hit it!

564
00:27:32,900 --> 00:27:34,000
- Here we go!
- Come on!

565
00:27:34,100 --> 00:27:36,733
[UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]

566
00:27:36,867 --> 00:27:38,000
[CROWD GASPING]

567
00:27:39,767 --> 00:27:41,700
[WHOOPING]

568
00:27:43,967 --> 00:27:50,900
[APPLAUSE, CHEERING]

569
00:27:51,100 --> 00:27:58,133
[UPBEAT MUSIC CONTINUES]

570
00:28:08,333 --> 00:28:11,967
[CHANTING] Tekla! Tekla!
Tekla! Tekla! Tekla!

571
00:28:12,133 --> 00:28:19,233
[TENDER MUSIC PLAYING]

572
00:28:19,333 --> 00:28:26,400
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
INSTRUMENTAL PLAYING]

573
00:28:31,967 --> 00:28:33,733
- Good job, Tekla!
- [CONFETTI POPS]

574
00:28:40,667 --> 00:28:47,633
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
INSTRUMENTAL CONTINUES]

575
00:29:01,400 --> 00:29:08,367
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
INSTRUMENTAL CONTINUES]

576
00:29:19,833 --> 00:29:20,667
[MOUTHS] So pretty!

577
00:29:20,833 --> 00:29:27,600
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
INSTRUMENTAL CONTINUES]

578
00:29:27,967 --> 00:29:29,700
You looks so beautiful.

579
00:29:32,033 --> 00:29:33,467
Thank you.

580
00:29:37,900 --> 00:29:40,200
[OVERLAPPING TEASING]

581
00:29:41,367 --> 00:29:47,667
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
INSTRUMENTAL CONTINUES]

582
00:29:47,767 --> 00:29:48,700
She didn't even bring cake!

583
00:29:48,900 --> 00:29:51,167
- Totally! Not like us!
- Yeah, we're way better!

584
00:29:51,367 --> 00:29:53,367
- You're the man, Gabo!
- They look perfect together!

585
00:30:01,433 --> 00:30:02,467
Come on.

586
00:30:02,633 --> 00:30:09,600
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
INSTRUMENTAL CONTINUES]

587
00:30:15,600 --> 00:30:17,700
<i>Max's sister has been missing
for two days.</i>

588
00:30:17,800 --> 00:30:18,400
<i> She's probably dead.</i>

589
00:30:18,600 --> 00:30:20,333
<i>- What did you say?!
- Ma'am!</i>

590
00:30:20,433 --> 00:30:22,900
<i>This is just the beginning
of the Zafras' downfall.</i>

591
00:30:23,067 --> 00:30:26,033
<i>Are we going to let him do
whatever he wants against us?</i>

592
00:30:26,133 --> 00:30:27,733
<i>I got this.
I know some people.</i>

593
00:30:27,900 --> 00:30:28,833
<i> So, what's your job for us?</i>

594
00:30:28,967 --> 00:30:31,067
<i>It's Rudy's birthday.
We'll pay them a visit.</i>

595
00:30:31,233 --> 00:30:32,167
<i> Life is hard enough.</i>

596
00:30:32,267 --> 00:30:33,867
<i>So if there's a reason
to be happy,</i>

597
00:30:34,033 --> 00:30:35,367
<i> we don't take it for granted.</i>

598
00:30:35,567 --> 00:30:37,400
<i>The people here
may not have much,</i>

599
00:30:37,500 --> 00:30:41,900
but we love and help each other
<i> no matter what.</i>
